# Sanitized nutrition-table fixtures for RealImageOcrTest are COMMITTED (2026-08-16), so CI cannot
# silently skip the highest-value regression tests. They are cropped to the nutrition panel only —
# no surroundings, no people, no unrelated packaging. Full-frame originals stay local.
app/src/androidTest/assets/ocr_real/originals/

# Full-frame source photographs for the OCR fixtures. Sanitized crops under
# app/src/androidTest/assets/ocr_real/ are committed; these originals never are.
Test labels/

# Scan evidence bundles pulled off a device for debugging. Debug builds only ever write these to
# app-private cache; a copy landing in the working tree is a local investigation artifact, and the
# repository is public. Diagnostics dumps quote recognized label text and can carry a capture.
#
# Matched case-insensitively and with any dated/numbered suffix, because each phone session arrives
# under its own name ("Scan Evidence 02-09 4th test", "Scan evidence 31-08-26", ...). The original
# rule named one exact path and matched none of them, which left ~700 MB of full-resolution
# photographs untracked-but-visible and one `git add -A` away from being public forever.
#
# What IS committed instead: the generated `*SessionFixtures.kt` files, which carry the recognized
# element text and geometry these bundles produced. That is the evidence the tests need; the
# photographs are not.
[Ss]can [Ee]vidence*/
docs/[Ss]can [Ee]vidence*/

# Brainstorming visual companion working files (local only)
.superpowers/
